============================================================
GIT MERGE DOCUMENTATION
DEVIL → MAIN
============================================================

Purpose:
This document explains the standard and safe process for merging
the "devil" branch into the "main" branch and pushing the result
to GitHub.

------------------------------------------------------------
1. CHECK CURRENT GIT STATUS
------------------------------------------------------------

Run:

git status

Check your current branch:

git branch

Example:

  backup-main
  develop1
  devil
* main

The "*" indicates the branch you are currently using.

------------------------------------------------------------
2. GET LATEST INFORMATION FROM GITHUB
------------------------------------------------------------

Always fetch the latest remote information first:

git fetch origin


------------------------------------------------------------
3. UPDATE THE DEVIL BRANCH
------------------------------------------------------------

Switch to devil:

git checkout devil

Pull the latest devil changes:

git pull origin devil


------------------------------------------------------------
4. UPDATE THE MAIN BRANCH
------------------------------------------------------------

Switch to main:

git checkout main

Pull the latest main changes:

git pull origin main


------------------------------------------------------------
5. MERGE DEVIL INTO MAIN
------------------------------------------------------------

Make sure you are on main:

git checkout main

Merge devil:

git merge devil


IMPORTANT:

The direction is:

DEVIL → MAIN

You must run:

git checkout main
git merge devil

Do NOT run:

git checkout devil
git merge devil


------------------------------------------------------------
6. IF THE MERGE IS SUCCESSFUL
------------------------------------------------------------

Git may show:

Fast-forward

OR:

Merge made by the 'ort' strategy.

After a successful merge, push main:

git push origin main


------------------------------------------------------------
7. IF GIT SAYS "ALREADY UP TO DATE"
------------------------------------------------------------

If you run:

git merge devil

and Git says:

Already up to date.

Check whether devil has commits that main does not have:

git log --oneline main..devil

If commits are displayed, devil has commits that are not in main.

You can also check the remote branches:

git fetch origin

git log --oneline origin/main..origin/devil

If nothing is displayed, Git considers the branches to contain
the same commits.


------------------------------------------------------------
8. CHECK DIFFERENCES BETWEEN DEVIL AND MAIN
------------------------------------------------------------

To see commit differences:

git log --oneline main..devil

To see file/code differences:

git diff main..devil

To see remote differences:

git diff origin/main..origin/devil


------------------------------------------------------------
9. MERGE CONFLICT
------------------------------------------------------------

Sometimes Git will show:

CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in some-file.ts

Automatic merge failed; fix conflicts and then commit the result.

Run:

git status

Git will show the conflicted files.

Example:

both modified: src/venue/venue.service.ts
both modified: src/venue/venue.controller.ts


------------------------------------------------------------
10. RESOLVE CONFLICTS IN VS CODE
------------------------------------------------------------

Open each conflicted file in VS Code.

You may see:

<<<<<<< HEAD

Code from main

=======

Code from devil

>>>>>>> devil


Meaning:

HEAD / Current Change = MAIN

Incoming Change = DEVIL


VS Code normally provides:

Accept Current Change
Accept Incoming Change
Accept Both Changes
Compare Changes


Choose the correct code based on the required application logic.

IMPORTANT:

Remove all conflict markers:

<<<<<<< HEAD
=======
>>>>>>> devil


------------------------------------------------------------
11. AFTER FIXING CONFLICTS
------------------------------------------------------------

Check the status:

git status

After fixing all conflicts, stage the files:

git add .


------------------------------------------------------------
12. COMPLETE THE MERGE
------------------------------------------------------------

Create the merge commit:

git commit -m "Merge devil into main"


Then push:

git push origin main


------------------------------------------------------------
13. IF YOU WANT TO CANCEL THE MERGE
------------------------------------------------------------

If the conflicts are too complicated or you want to cancel
the current merge:

git merge --abort

Then check:

git status

This returns the repository to the state before the merge.


------------------------------------------------------------
14. IMPORTANT: REBASE IN PROGRESS
------------------------------------------------------------

If Git says:

interactive rebase in progress

and:

No commands remaining.

You are currently editing a commit while rebasing.

If everything is correct:

git rebase --continue

If you want to cancel the rebase:

git rebase --abort


IMPORTANT:

Finish or abort an active rebase before starting a normal merge.


------------------------------------------------------------
15. COMPLETE SAFE MERGE PROCESS
------------------------------------------------------------

Use this process when merging devil into main:

STEP 1:

git fetch origin


STEP 2:

git checkout devil


STEP 3:

git pull origin devil


STEP 4:

git checkout main


STEP 5:

git pull origin main


STEP 6:

git merge devil


STEP 7:

If there are conflicts:

git status

Fix the conflicts in VS Code.


STEP 8:

git add .


STEP 9:

git commit -m "Merge devil into main"


STEP 10:

git push origin main


------------------------------------------------------------
16. DAILY DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW
------------------------------------------------------------

MORNING:

Update main:

git checkout main
git pull origin main


Update devil:

git checkout devil
git pull origin devil


------------------------------------------------------------
DURING DEVELOPMENT
------------------------------------------------------------

Work on the devil branch.

After making changes:

git status

git add .

git commit -m "Update latest changes"

git push origin devil


------------------------------------------------------------
EVENING / RELEASE
------------------------------------------------------------

Switch to main:

git checkout main

Update main:

git pull origin main

Merge devil:

git merge devil

Push main:

git push origin main


------------------------------------------------------------
17. IMPORTANT TEAM RULE
------------------------------------------------------------

Before merging devil into main:

ALWAYS:

git checkout main
git pull origin main
git merge devil
git push origin main


Do not force push main for normal merge operations.

Avoid:

git push --force


Use normal:

git push origin main


------------------------------------------------------------
18. CHECK BEFORE MERGING
------------------------------------------------------------

Check current branch:

git branch

Check status:

git status

Check commits in devil but not main:

git log --oneline main..devil

Check code differences:

git diff main..devil


------------------------------------------------------------
19. IF DEVIL IS UPDATED ON GITHUB BUT LOCAL DEVIL IS OLD
------------------------------------------------------------

Run:

git fetch origin

git checkout devil

git pull origin devil

Then:

git checkout main

git pull origin main

git merge devil

git push origin main


------------------------------------------------------------
20. FINAL CHEAT SHEET
------------------------------------------------------------

Update devil:

git fetch origin
git checkout devil
git pull origin devil


Update main:

git checkout main
git pull origin main


Merge:

git merge devil


If conflict:

git status

Fix conflicts in VS Code.

Then:

git add .

git commit -m "Merge devil into main"


Push:

git push origin main


------------------------------------------------------------
21. MERGE DIRECTION
------------------------------------------------------------

The required merge direction is:

                DEVIL
                  |
                  |
                  | git merge devil
                  ↓
                 MAIN
                  |
                  |
                  | git push origin main
                  ↓
              GITHUB MAIN


------------------------------------------------------------
22. MOST IMPORTANT COMMANDS
------------------------------------------------------------

git fetch origin

git checkout devil

git pull origin devil

git checkout main

git pull origin main

git merge devil

git status

git add .

git commit -m "Merge devil into main"

git push origin main


